+## Canonical UI terminology
+
+The German labels below record the accepted wording from [#469](https://github.com/Grabman1987/budget/issues/469), including the owner's [allocation terms](https://github.com/Grabman1987/budget/issues/469#issuecomment-6209535836) and [single-category and Gespart clarification](https://github.com/Grabman1987/budget/issues/469#issuecomment-6213536356). They supersede conflicting historical UI wording in this document; dated directives remain as history. Financial meaning and calculations still follow `SPEC.md` and the existing shared models.
+
+- **Kategorie** replaces visible “Envelope”; technical identifiers may retain `envelope`.
+- **Verplantes Geld** replaces the UI label “Verfügbar in Envelopes”. This is a wording mapping, not a new calculation or a replacement for every use of “Verfügbar”.
+- **Ausgabentempo** replaces visible “Pace”; the existing metric and period contract remain unchanged.
+- **Noch im Plan** replaces the UI label “Plan-Rest”.
+- **Zu verteilen** is the lead figure in Plan, Heute and the corresponding reports, replacing “Noch zu verplanen”.
+- **Zugewiesen** names the category assignment column. This does not rename unrelated concepts such as “Geplante Zahlung”.
+- **Verteilen** names distributing “Zu verteilen” across multiple categories. **Zuweisen** remains appropriate for one category, including “Rate zuweisen” and “Schnell zuweisen”.
+- **Sparziel** denotes a target amount by a date; **Monatsziel** denotes the monthly rate. These names do not introduce another target type or change target calculations.
+- **Gespart**, in the wealth-development measure chain, replaces “Eigenleistung”: **Einnahmen − Konsum + reguläre Tilgung**, so **Anfang + Gespart + Markt = Jetzt**. This is the existing wealth contract, not a new formula or a definition for unrelated savings measures.
+- **Allokation** replaces visible “Allocation”.
+
+The [page review](docs/product/page-review-2026-10-16.md) also records newer route and navigation wording, including “Prüfen” instead of “Posteingang”. Under [#529](https://github.com/Grabman1987/budget/issues/529), apply terminology in each owning page task, not a separate app-wide replacement sweep. This glossary records the agreed vocabulary; it does not certify that every visible string has been updated or that #469's browser and delivery acceptance is complete.
+
 ## Platform
 
 Owner directive PR2 (2026-10-04): stored Regelwerk risk thresholds supply Portfolio, report 4.2, rebalancing, savings recommendations and Heute/finance check through one resolver. Leveraged ETFs count in speculative/cluster risk; market value and gross exposure stay distinct. Stored class bands override the smaller-of-5-percentage-points/25%-of-target standard. Historical parameter/leverage versioning remains outside this slice. See [risk policy](docs/portfolio-risk-policy.md).
